    "canonical_title": "Show HN 帖子介绍 Context Diet：一个通过 Claude Code JS Hook API 在工具结果写入对话前进行摘要剪裁的 mod",
    "category": "developer_tools",
    "credibility_score": 0.4,
    "entity_names": [
      "Context Diet",
      "Claude Code",
      "Anthropic",
      "jest",
      "vitest",
      "pytest",
      "go test",
      "cargo",
      "tsc",
      "eslint",
      "docker build"
    ],
    "evidence_ids": [
      "5264b52a1d56b7e5a20a0de2"
    ],
    "facts": [
      "作者在 Hacker News 发布 Show HN 帖子，介绍其构建的 Context Diet，用于解决长时间 Claude Code 会话中工具输出占满上下文的问题。",
      "作者称单次冗长的测试运行或构建日志可达 30–50k 字符，其中几乎全是 PASSED 行、警告和 lockfile 变动。",
      "作者称 Context Diet 是一个 mod，使用 Claude Code 新的 JS hook API，在工具结果被存入对话之前重写它们。",
      "作者称对测试运行器和构建工具（jest、vitest、pytest、go test、cargo、tsc、eslint、npm/pip install、docker build）会解析出摘要：每个失败及其消息和位置，加上汇总；通过的测试只计数、不逐条列出。",
      "作者称 JSON 会变成骨架，diff 丢弃 lockfile 变动，grep 结果和文件列表会被分组，表格保留精确的首行和末行。",
      "作者称重复运行同一命令时只显示变化部分。",
      "作者称完整输出始终保存到文件，摘要会说明位置，以便代理在需要更多信息时读取。",
      "作者称在 7 个有已知答案的问答任务上，两组均为 7/7，工具调用为 8 次而非 13 次。",
      "作者称在一个 bug 修复任务（600 个测试、两个隐藏 bug，Haiku/Sonnet/Opus，18 次运行）中，每个代理无论是否使用该工具都修复了两个 bug，工具调用为 6 次而非 8 次。",
      "作者给出保留意见：在非常大的输出上 token 节省有限，因为 Claude Code 已经会把这类输出移到文件；收益在于步骤更少。",
      "作者称当命令失败时，Claude Code 只保留约 10k 字符并丢弃输出末尾，而失败通常就在那里。",
      "作者称有一个可选模式会保存更多内容（帖子原文在此处被截断）。"
    ],
    "grounded_analysis": [],
    "id": "story-63fef70f17b9424d122c",
    "importance_score": 0.45,
    "novelty_score": 0.62,
    "opinions": [
      "作者表示最关心的问题是它是否会让代理变差，并称上述测试结果让他相信不会。",
      "作者主动给出保留意见，称 token 节省在超大输出上有限，因为 Claude Code 已将其移到文件，收益是步骤更少。"
    ],
    "primary_source_url": "https://github.com/drkokorev/context-diet",
    "product_names": [
      "Context Diet",
      "Claude Code"
    ],
    "published_at": "2026-10-09T18:18:26Z",
    "relevance_score": 0.82,
    "source_item_ids": [
      "item-0652c1bf572d27f0f7b7"
    ],
    "source_materials": [
      {
        "association_basis": "story_input",
        "content_excerpt": "Hi HN, I built this after watching long Claude Code sessions fill up with tool output: a single verbose test run or build log can be 30–50k characters, almost all of it PASSED lines, warnings and lockfile churn. The context fills, compaction comes sooner, and the agent forgets earlier instructions. Context Diet is a mod (Claude Code's new JS hook API) that rewrites tool results before they are stored in the conversation: - test runners and build tools (jest, vitest, pytest, go test, cargo, tsc, eslint, npm/pip install, docker build) get parsed digests: every failure with its message and location, plus the summary; passing tests are counted, not listed - JSON becomes a skeleton, diffs drop lockfile churn, grep results and file lists are grouped, tables keep exact first and last rows - running the same command again shows only what changed - the full output is always saved to a file, and the digest says where, so the agent can read it when it needs more The question I cared about most was whether it makes the agent worse. On 7 Q&A tasks with known answers, both groups were 7/7, with 8 tool calls instead of 13. On a bug-fixing task (600 tests, two hidden bugs, Haiku/Sonnet/Opus, 18 runs) every agent fixed both bugs with or without it, using 6 tool calls instead of 8. Honest caveats: the token saving on very large outputs is modest, because Claude Code already moves those to a file; the gain there is fewer steps. Also, when a command fails, Claude Code keeps only ~10k characters and drops the end of the output, where the failures usually are. There is an opt-in mode that saves",
        "content_missing": false,
        "content_version": null,
        "date_precision": null,
